WEBVTT

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:16.850
Abiru hodo dakiattari kuchizuke shitari

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:23.056
Abiru hodo kenka shitari aishiattari

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:29.263
Ari no mama omae no koto shiritai kuse ni

00:00:29.263 --> 00:00:35.002
Ari no mama nante narenai ore no hou sa

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:38.138
Wakaranai

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.874
Omae no kokoro ga

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:42.876
Nazedayo

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:47.514
Honto wa majutsushi kai?

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:51.685
Dakishimetai

00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:55.289
Hitori ja cry

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:59.960
Mou nido to hitori ja itakunai

00:01:01.295 --> 00:01:04.298
Dakishimetai

00:01:04.298 --> 00:01:07.601
Omae to fly

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:15.375
Marude naiteru youna kanjiteru koe ni toketeiku

00:01:15.876 --> 00:01:21.882
Serenade

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:36.763
Spire of the Sun, that I build!

00:01:41.635 --> 00:01:42.903
Majic...

00:01:44.805 --> 00:01:48.175
Geez, you can't even set fire to a dry twig?

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:50.510
But I'm just an apprentice.

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:53.780
Where Rocks Row is...

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.118
through the valley of Yuginia by crossing
the Sun Lake Mountain is the shortest way?

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.591
| warn you.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
Do not hinder me, Krylancelo.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.664
Should you prove a hindrance again,
I shall kill you.

00:02:10.664 --> 00:02:12.232
| thought I told you.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:15.135
I'll save Azalie, without fail!

00:02:17.738 --> 00:02:19.039
Childman!

00:02:20.107 --> 00:02:23.210
What are you mulling about by yourself?

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:27.114
If you've got so much free time,
then find us lodging somewhere!

00:02:28.749 --> 00:02:31.351
Geez, you sure don't get bored of it, do you?

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.420
Saying the same thing everyday?

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.890
This time I want to sleep
in a place with a decent bed

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.726
and a bathtub that doesn't have spiders!

00:02:40.327 --> 00:02:44.131
Master, look at this!

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.467
You're kidding! The stone's burning!

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:51.438
Isn't it amazing! This is my magic isn't it?

00:02:51.438 --> 00:02:52.439
Right? Right?

00:02:53.507 --> 00:02:58.712
What magic? This is an honest
to goodness piece of coal!

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:03.517
Leki, you see, this is what they call coal.
It's a rock that burns.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:29.609
MEMORY YOU CAN'T SURPASS

00:03:33.547 --> 00:03:36.516
Wow! This is the first time
I've ever seen anything like this!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.089
Come to think about it, I've heard of this.

00:03:42.089 --> 00:03:46.827
In addition to iron and steel,
they mine coal at Sun Lake Mountain.

00:03:50.664 --> 00:03:52.666
Didn't we learn this in school?

00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:55.068
That's why the town grew here.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.336
Is that so?

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.638
We're going.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.184
Wow!

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:14.321
It seems that there would be
decent lodgings here, right?

00:04:14.321 --> 00:04:16.356
That might be pushing it.

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.893
This isn't a place where
strangers like us can kick back.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.229
Is that so?

00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:29.736
Leki, they call that a lamp,

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:34.040
and it's much more useful than
Orphen or Majic's magic.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:37.878
Wait a minute! Don't lump me in with Majic!

00:04:37.878 --> 00:04:41.248
Master, even I can do a little...

00:04:41.248 --> 00:04:45.185
If you got a complaint, why don't you
just bring out a single flame?

00:04:45.185 --> 00:04:46.520
Magic, you say?

00:04:48.522 --> 00:04:50.957
You all, are you sorcerers?

00:04:51.725 --> 00:04:55.328
This... Doesn't this feel really bad?

00:04:55.929 --> 00:04:57.798
Violence isn't good.

00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:59.966
If we talk, you'll understand. If we talk!

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.035
Well, we're asking you if you are!

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.005
And if we are, then what?

00:05:14.581 --> 00:05:16.316
Welcome to Sun Lake!

00:05:18.752 --> 00:05:20.554
What's going on?

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:34.367
You must be tired!
Please work hard tomorrow too!

00:05:35.202 --> 00:05:37.838
Madam, thanks for everything!

00:05:37.838 --> 00:05:39.072
Sure!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.842
Madam! Cox!

00:05:42.309 --> 00:05:44.311
I've got amazing guests!

00:05:44.311 --> 00:05:47.414
Guests? Who is it, dear?

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.785
Listen and be surprised.

00:05:52.219 --> 00:05:54.588
It's one group of sorcerers!

00:05:57.958 --> 00:06:00.493
Hey, what does all this mean?

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.329
Don't ask me.

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.299
As if I'd know, either!

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.803
Sorcerers...

00:06:15.175 --> 00:06:17.510
A sorcerer saved this town?

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:20.947
Yeah, that was about ten years ago though.

00:06:21.982 --> 00:06:24.851
| don't even want to remember it.
It was that bad of an accident.

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:28.788
And the one who saved our guys
trapped inside the mine

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:31.057
was a traveling sorcerer.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.127
With just his own magic?

00:06:34.294 --> 00:06:36.563
Well, they come in all levels, right?

00:06:36.563 --> 00:06:39.666
Who'd believe that sorcerers
could be so different?

00:06:39.666 --> 00:06:41.234
Leave me alone!

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:46.406
You guys, if you don't have a place to stay,
you may as well stay here.

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:48.174
We have open rooms, so...

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:50.443
Really? All right!

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.678
Are you sure it's okay?

00:06:51.678 --> 00:06:56.583
Oh, I don't mind at all, because in this town
sorcerers are lifesavers.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:59.886
It's been so long! Bath! Bed!

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.755
It's like a dream!

00:07:02.122 --> 00:07:04.157
Well, aren't you making a big deal of it?

00:07:05.125 --> 00:07:09.930
But if there is such a powerful sorcerer,
I'd like to meet him.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.332
| know that sorcerer's name.

00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:13.867
Really?

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.536
He told only me.

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.638
And what's his name?

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.573
He's called Childman.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.185
Childman...

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:48.435
Now honey, you hold off on smoking
till the afternoon, hear?

00:07:48.435 --> 00:07:51.338
| know that! I'm not a kid, you know.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.039
Morning!

00:07:56.009 --> 00:08:00.013
Orphen, we're going to take
a walk around here, okay?

00:08:00.013 --> 00:08:01.014
Sure.

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.286
Mister Orphen,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.855
did you sleep well last night?

00:08:09.356 --> 00:08:10.490
So-so.

00:08:11.091 --> 00:08:15.462
But I'm so thrilled!
| get to meet a sorcerer again!

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.732
Was he that amazing?

00:08:18.732 --> 00:08:21.668
That sorcerer called Childman?

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:24.104
Yeah, of course!

00:08:24.404 --> 00:08:29.109
| was only five, so you really can't
depend on my impressions.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:33.980
But I remember the circumstances very clearly.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.316
It was my dad, you see...

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:40.587
that got caught in the accident ten years ago.

00:08:44.124 --> 00:08:47.293
| heard that my dad got left behind
by himself in the mining tunnel.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.897
| begged him, "Please save my dad!"

00:08:51.798 --> 00:08:55.869
| just felt that that he could save him.

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:05.645
Mister Orphen?

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:18.625
Not reflecting on the dangers to his own life,

00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:22.262
the unnamed sorcerer saved the lives
and future of Sun Lake.

00:09:22.262 --> 00:09:25.698
To his miracle we dedicate this fountain.

00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:28.201
Saved the future?

00:09:28.835 --> 00:09:33.606
It's sort of cool that he did that
and didn't leave his name.

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:38.778
He was a really great sorcerer after all,
that Childman person.

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:42.082
Well, he is Master's Master, after all!

00:09:42.816 --> 00:09:46.519
Miracle? Or was it just a whim?

00:09:48.822 --> 00:09:50.090
Childman...

00:09:53.827 --> 00:09:56.196
Aren't you a sorcerer?

00:09:56.463 --> 00:09:57.564
Y-yeah.

00:09:57.564 --> 00:09:59.099
| thought so.

00:09:59.099 --> 00:10:03.336
My mom said that we have
electricity and water

00:10:03.336 --> 00:10:06.940
because a long time ago
a sorcerer found coal for us.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:09.742
So, show us some magic!

00:10:18.251 --> 00:10:19.652
Orphen...

00:10:21.087 --> 00:10:22.288
What?

00:10:23.556 --> 00:10:26.326
Cheap! Cheap! Why won't you?

00:10:28.428 --> 00:10:32.632
Hey, I'll show you some magic,
so just let him go, okay?

00:10:33.433 --> 00:10:34.434
Really?

00:10:34.434 --> 00:10:36.703
Are you a sorcerer too?

00:10:36.703 --> 00:10:38.037
That's right.

00:10:39.506 --> 00:10:42.142
Spire of the Sun, that I build!

00:10:48.715 --> 00:10:50.650
Fake!

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.219
This guy's not a sorcerer!

00:10:53.453 --> 00:10:54.687
Fake! Fake!

00:10:55.221 --> 00:10:58.391
Kids are really honest, after all, aren't they?

00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:03.496
My image of a sorcerer is crumbling.

00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:06.833
| know I'm still in my apprenticeship, but...

00:11:06.833 --> 00:11:08.735
No! It's not that!

00:11:10.036 --> 00:11:13.206
| thought he was like him, but...

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.441
Like him?

00:11:32.559 --> 00:11:34.861
Okay! How about lunch then?

00:11:34.861 --> 00:11:35.428
Yeah!

00:11:35.428 --> 00:11:36.496
I'm so hungry!
Yeah!

00:11:36.496 --> 00:11:37.430
I'm so hungry!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.799
| can finally take a smoke!

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:42.502
They warned us about it again
this morning too, didn't they?

00:11:42.502 --> 00:11:46.072
We already know fire's not allowed in here!

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.479
Okay, the nuisances are gone.

00:11:54.681 --> 00:12:00.019
Say, I think your idea is a little
too far-fetched, Big Brother.

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:01.621
What are you saying, Dortin?!

00:12:01.621 --> 00:12:06.326
If they have a burning rock, then it's
only natural to have an edible rock.

00:12:06.326 --> 00:12:08.695
I think it's really unnatural.

00:12:08.695 --> 00:12:11.598
Okay, then from somewhere around here.

00:12:12.332 --> 00:12:13.933
It's kinda dark.

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:15.802
Hey, Dortin, the lamp!

00:12:16.002 --> 00:12:20.240
But Big Brother, earlier they said
that fire's not allowed,

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.142
so shouldn't we hurry up and put this out?

00:12:23.142 --> 00:12:25.111
Shut up! Hurry up and do it!

00:12:25.111 --> 00:12:29.215
Keep stalling and I'll kill you
by choking you with a firefly's light!

00:12:35.321 --> 00:12:37.690
That hurts.

00:13:10.456 --> 00:13:12.992
It's been a while, Krylancelo.

00:13:12.992 --> 00:13:15.762
You both still want Azalie's life!

00:13:15.762 --> 00:13:17.864
The command of the Tower of Fangs is absolute.

00:13:17.864 --> 00:13:19.499
What command?

00:13:19.499 --> 00:13:22.168
It's only for your precious honor, isn't it?

00:13:23.102 --> 00:13:24.404
That's right.

00:13:25.772 --> 00:13:27.173
Childman...

00:13:28.308 --> 00:13:30.810
which one's the real you?

00:13:38.217 --> 00:13:39.419
What?

00:13:41.854 --> 00:13:43.556
Is it an earthquake?

00:13:44.524 --> 00:13:45.692
That is...

00:13:55.001 --> 00:13:58.438
Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:13:58.905 --> 00:14:02.608
Who is it?! Who dares try to BBQ me to death?!

00:14:02.608 --> 00:14:03.810
It's not like that!

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:06.045
It's because you knocked over
the lamp, Big Brother!

00:14:06.045 --> 00:14:09.048
What'd you say? You're the one who dropped it!

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:10.383
But that's...!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.552
Get away quickly!

00:14:12.552 --> 00:14:13.753
Get away!

00:14:13.753 --> 00:14:16.255
Hurry up and get away!
You'll be engulfed!

00:14:17.156 --> 00:14:19.325
Is there anyone left inside?

00:14:19.325 --> 00:14:22.228
I think I heard someone's voice,
just at the time of the explosion,

00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:23.996
but I don't know anything more than that!

00:14:24.397 --> 00:14:25.898
There're people inside?

00:14:55.628 --> 00:15:00.266
Legendary Sorcerer, please save our fathers!

00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:02.268
Childman!

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:06.172
Towers of Heaven, that dance around me!

00:15:14.313 --> 00:15:17.083
It's no good. The flames are
burning too strongly!

00:15:17.083 --> 00:15:18.351
Damn!

00:15:20.052 --> 00:15:21.220
You!

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.256
I'll do something about this.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:33.499
So, is this what they call fate?

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.501
But...

00:15:36.369 --> 00:15:38.671
| won't follow in your footsteps anymore!

00:15:39.238 --> 00:15:41.340
I'll rise above you!

00:15:42.108 --> 00:15:44.610
Sisters of Explosion, that I cry out!

00:15:49.215 --> 00:15:51.918
| guess I can't just blow it out.

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:57.657
Wall of Earth, that I sharpen!

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:31.924
He did it! It's out!

00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:33.759
Now we can relax.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.394
The fire's out!

00:16:35.394 --> 00:16:36.729
Master!

00:16:37.263 --> 00:16:41.567
How about it, Cox? Just like Childman-

00:16:48.107 --> 00:16:49.542
But that's...

00:16:49.842 --> 00:16:51.143
It's exactly the same.

00:16:59.952 --> 00:17:02.088
As what happened ten years ago.

00:17:07.527 --> 00:17:08.861
Master!

00:17:08.861 --> 00:17:10.029
Orphen!

00:17:11.464 --> 00:17:14.767
There's still got to be a way.

00:17:17.303 --> 00:17:18.971
More than those flames...

00:17:19.605 --> 00:17:24.143
For a second the mountain lit up
brighter than the flames.

00:17:24.477 --> 00:17:25.611
What's that?

00:17:25.611 --> 00:17:26.913
What do you mean?

00:17:29.048 --> 00:17:30.650
You guys hurry up and take cover!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:31.584
Orphen?!

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:54.273
Sword of Light, whom I do release!

00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:35.147
Whoa, he did it!

00:18:35.147 --> 00:18:36.148
It's gone!

00:18:36.148 --> 00:18:37.550
Now's our chance!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:38.918
Let's go!

00:18:38.918 --> 00:18:40.987
Hurry!

00:18:42.855 --> 00:18:44.790
You did it, didn't you, Master?

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:46.792
How in the world did you do that?

00:18:47.293 --> 00:18:49.795
| blew the flames out with the blast.

00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:50.863
Huh?!

00:18:50.863 --> 00:18:52.498
So how about it, Cox?

00:18:52.498 --> 00:18:54.600
Isn't my master amazing too?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.501
Yeah.

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:03.142
| haven't excelled him at all.

00:19:04.644 --> 00:19:08.147
| only mimicked the miracle
of ten years past.

00:19:08.648 --> 00:19:10.016
Everyone's all right!

00:19:10.016 --> 00:19:11.651
I'm so thankful!

00:19:12.385 --> 00:19:13.619
That's great!

00:19:13.953 --> 00:19:15.254
That's great!

00:19:19.725 --> 00:19:23.162
Mister Sorcerer, everyone was
saved because of you!

00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:26.499
| haven't excelled him at all.

00:19:27.767 --> 00:19:29.101
Childman...

00:19:30.202 --> 00:19:31.504
Master!

00:19:33.272 --> 00:19:35.074
Mister Sorcerer,

00:19:35.074 --> 00:19:38.778
thank you for saving our dads!

00:19:40.346 --> 00:19:42.248
See, didn't I tell you?

00:19:42.248 --> 00:19:45.084
Even though he's got evil eyes,
he's a good sorcerer!

00:19:45.084 --> 00:19:48.621
Yeah! You can't judge people
by the way they look, can you?

00:19:49.555 --> 00:19:52.625
Hey, they called you, Orphen didn't they?

00:19:53.959 --> 00:19:55.494
Okay, go!

00:19:55.494 --> 00:19:57.663
Thank you, Orphen!

00:20:00.466 --> 00:20:02.735
Thank you!
Hey! Quit it!

00:20:02.735 --> 00:20:03.369
What are you doing?

00:20:03.369 --> 00:20:04.704
Thank you!
What are you doing?

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:06.672
What are you doing?

00:20:07.406 --> 00:20:08.340
Hey!

00:20:10.776 --> 00:20:11.644
Hey!

00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:17.983
Thank you, Mister Childman!

00:20:18.484 --> 00:20:20.119
| need no thanks.

00:20:20.119 --> 00:20:22.154
| only did what should be done.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.129
Hey, just a minute! I said go away!

00:20:30.129 --> 00:20:31.997
What are you so embarrassed about?

00:20:31.997 --> 00:20:35.501
It's not that! I said I don't need any thanks!

00:20:35.501 --> 00:20:37.103
He is like him after all.

00:20:37.103 --> 00:20:38.437
Please go away!

00:20:38.437 --> 00:20:41.173
Like Mister Childman, ten years ago!

00:20:41.173 --> 00:20:42.675
Of course!

00:20:42.675 --> 00:20:45.878
After all, he was my master's master!

00:20:48.781 --> 00:20:52.184
If it wasn't for that thing with Miss Azalie,

00:20:52.184 --> 00:20:54.186
Don't pull that!
they would have been together even now.

00:20:54.186 --> 00:20:55.521
They would have been together even now.

00:20:57.490 --> 00:21:00.693
Majic, don't just watch! Do something!

00:21:00.693 --> 00:21:02.194
No, please do something!

00:21:02.194 --> 00:21:03.929
If you don't, you're anathemal!

00:21:03.929 --> 00:21:05.064
Yes!

00:21:06.599 --> 00:21:07.933
Okay everyone, personal space!

00:21:07.933 --> 00:21:09.034
Hurry up, Majic!

00:21:09.034 --> 00:21:10.603
Don't be so happy!

00:21:17.309 --> 00:21:19.311
| have just received word.

00:21:19.745 --> 00:21:21.914
It seems the fire at Sun Lake Mountain

00:21:21.914 --> 00:21:25.417
was miraculously extinguished
by a single sorcerer.

00:21:26.152 --> 00:21:27.920
This most probably is...

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.388
| am aware.

00:22:04.456 --> 00:22:05.858
Krylancelo...

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:19.104
